content:
Recommend an Ollama model for this host.

Available RAM: {{ram_gb | number:min=1:max=128:placeholder="16":required}}
Use case: {{use_case | select:options=["General","Coding","Reasoning","Vision","Small / fastest"]:default="General":required}}
GPU: {{gpu | select:options=["NVIDIA","AMD","Apple Silicon","CPU-only","Not sure"]:default="Not sure"}}

Use the `ollama_hardware_detect` tool if the GPU is "Not sure", then call `ollama_recommend_model` with the RAM and use case. Present the top 3 options with expected tokens/second and the pull command for each. End with a one-line recommendation of the best fit.

Pull a model into the Ollama server.

Model name: {{model_name | text:placeholder="e.g. llama3.2:1b":required}}
Confirm I understand pulls can be large: {{confirm | checkbox:label="I understand the download size":required}}

Before pulling, call `ollama_list_models` to check if the model is already pulled. If it is, report that and stop. If not, warn the user about the approximate size (small models ~1-2GB, 7B models ~4-5GB, larger models 10GB+), then call `ollama_pull_model` with the model name. Report the result with the model name and status.

Help clean up Ollama models to free disk space.

Action: {{action | select:options=["List only","Remove a specific model","Remove all unused"]:default="List only":required}}
Model to remove (if applicable): {{model_name | text:placeholder="e.g. qwen2.5:0.5b"}}

Call `ollama_list_models` to show all pulled models with sizes. If the action is "Remove a specific model", ask the user to confirm the exact model name, then call `ollama_delete_model` with `confirm=True` only after explicit confirmation in the chat. If the action is "Remove all unused", list the models and ask which ones to remove one by one. Never delete without explicit per-model confirmation.

Summarize the Ollama session telemetry.

Focus: {{focus | select:options=["Latest session","Per-model aggregates","Peak resource usage","All"]:default="Latest session":required}}

Load the `telemetry-reader` skill via `view_skill` to get the interpretation framework. Then explain what the user should look for based on their focus choice, and tell them which `task` command to run (`task sessions`, `task watch`, or `task sessions -- <session_id>`). Do not fabricate telemetry numbers — if you do not have the data, say so and point to the command that produces it.
